{"id": "d2c08437-0b19-4f75-bb32-900db6fbb0a6", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm recalling that synchronous Textract calls like AnalyzeDocument differ from async ones in how they access S3 — Textract doesn't assume an IAM role to read S3 objects directly for synchronous requests, unlike StartDocumentAnalysis which does. That distinction is likely the root of the AccessDenied issue the user is hitting.

I should verify this precisely using verify_aws_claim, since the key question is whether the S3 GetObject call for synchronous AnalyzeDocument is made under the calling IAM identity's permissions or a Textract-assumed service role. My recollection is that sync APIs don't accept a RoleArn at all, so the caller's own credentials need the S3 permissions - meaning the likely gap is on the caller identity, not a separate service role.

"}]}

